DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T230000
DTSTAMP:20260910T195312Z
CREATED:20260522T123013Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260910T195312Z
UID:50187-1791057600-1791068400@beachmetro.com
SUMMARY:Tanglefoot Reunion
DESCRIPTION:The Songs\, The Stories\, The Spirit of Canada \nFor three decades\, Tanglefoot carried the spirit of Canada across stages in North America\, the United Kingdom\, and Europe with powerful harmonies\, quick wit\, rich storytelling\, and songs rooted in Canadian history. Now this legendary Canadian folk ensemble returns for a special reunion concert\, bringing their unmistakable energy\, warmth\, and humour back to the stage. \nThis new chapter reunites Canadian Folk Music Award winners Steve Ritchie\, Al Parrish\, Sandra Swannell Young\, and Rob Ritchie\, joined by Rob’s son\, singer and multi-instrumentalist Josh Ritchie\, stepping into the place once held by the late Terry Young. It is both a celebration of legacy and a fresh passing of the torch. \nAudiences can expect fan favourites\, hidden gems\, stories\, laughter\, and the kind of heartfelt music that turns a concert into a shared memory. For longtime fans\, this is a rare chance to reconnect with a beloved part of Canadian folk music. For those discovering Tanglefoot for the first time\, it is an invitation into songs that feel timeless\, spirited\, and deeply Canadian. \nJoin us at Acoustic Harvest for an evening of friendship\, storytelling\, and music that reminds us why live folk music still matters.
URL:https://beachmetro.com/event/tanglefoot-reunion/
LOCATION:Acoustic Harvest\, 200 McIntosh Street\, Scarborough
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://d28bcn7yu97icd.cloudfront.net/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/22083015/event62051.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Acoustic Harvest":MAILTO:acousticharvest@proton.me
END:VEVENT
